WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.336
[♪ theme music playing]

00:24.316 --> 00:26.944
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

00:29.029 --> 00:30.530
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES,
ORGANIZATIONS, ETC. ARE FICTIONAL

00:30.614 --> 00:31.949
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

00:32.032 --> 00:33.951
ANIMALS WERE FILMED
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE RULES

00:34.034 --> 00:35.577
[♪ gentle pop music playing]

00:37.871 --> 00:39.373
YOUNGSOOK'S RESTAURANT

00:51.301 --> 00:52.302
CEO YOO MERI

00:54.596 --> 00:55.722
[line ringing]

01:09.570 --> 01:10.571
[line ringing]

01:11.488 --> 01:12.656
[phone vibrating]

01:18.370 --> 01:19.830
Hey, did you find it?

01:19.913 --> 01:20.914
[Wooju] It's me.

01:22.583 --> 01:23.584
How have you been?

01:24.209 --> 01:25.669
[♪ gripping dramatic music playing]

01:27.212 --> 01:28.213
I'm back.

01:28.297 --> 01:29.298
I'm in Seoul.

01:29.923 --> 01:31.508
-As soon as I landed...
-[line disconnects]

01:32.426 --> 01:33.552
Hello? Hel...

01:40.309 --> 01:41.310
[line connects]

01:41.977 --> 01:44.688
[automated voice] The call can't
be connected. Transferring to voicemail.

01:44.771 --> 01:46.982
You will be charged after the tone.

01:47.065 --> 01:48.191
[line disconnects]

01:48.275 --> 01:49.401
Sure.

01:49.484 --> 01:51.320
You must have some pride in yourself.

01:51.820 --> 01:53.071
Play hard to get once.

01:56.283 --> 01:57.409
WOOJU

01:58.160 --> 01:59.161
That scared me.

02:01.288 --> 02:03.123
He told me never to call him.

02:05.375 --> 02:06.376
[gasps]

02:08.670 --> 02:09.921
Why did he call me?

02:10.589 --> 02:11.798
Does he know something?

02:16.178 --> 02:17.429
TEAM LEADER KIM WOOJU

02:19.181 --> 02:20.265
[phone vibrating]

02:24.603 --> 02:25.604
Hello?

02:26.355 --> 02:27.356
I found it.

02:27.939 --> 02:29.441
It was in the door gap.

02:29.524 --> 02:31.151
Oh, that's a relief.

02:32.903 --> 02:36.490
No, I'll come and get it.
I have a meeting there anyway.

02:38.158 --> 02:39.326
Oh, and...

02:40.243 --> 02:42.871
Should I tell him that Wooju called?

02:43.622 --> 02:45.749
What is it? Do you have something to say?

02:46.792 --> 02:49.002
No, I'll see you tomorrow.

02:51.171 --> 02:52.172
[line disconnects]

02:58.178 --> 03:00.681
I shouldn't bother him for no reason.

03:02.349 --> 03:03.725
I feel bad about everything already.

03:10.273 --> 03:11.358
[exhales deeply]

03:17.989 --> 03:18.990
Are you still up?

03:19.616 --> 03:21.743
Yes, I couldn't sleep.

03:22.369 --> 03:23.412
Were you out somewhere?

03:23.495 --> 03:25.705
-Oh, at the garage.
-I see.

03:26.373 --> 03:27.374
How is work?

03:27.457 --> 03:30.085
You don't work for fun. You just work.

03:30.168 --> 03:31.169
What?

03:31.253 --> 03:32.504
[both chuckle]

03:33.130 --> 03:34.965
I'm a total workaholic these days.

03:35.048 --> 03:38.051
I have no work-life balance,
and I'm completely committed.

03:39.010 --> 03:42.889
You should relax
now that Uncle and I are around.

03:42.973 --> 03:44.683
Go on trips and dates.

03:45.600 --> 03:47.144
Enjoy life a bit.

03:47.227 --> 03:48.687
Why would I go on dates?

03:48.770 --> 03:51.273
[chuckles softly] I'd abandon my husband
if I had one.

03:51.898 --> 03:54.025
Look at all the old women who are happy.

03:54.109 --> 03:55.610
They're all widows.

03:56.278 --> 03:58.613
Only those with their husbands alive
look glum and distraught.

03:59.239 --> 04:02.075
By the way, if you have anybody,
bring her to see me.

04:02.159 --> 04:04.786
Someone worthy of marrying
the head of Myungsoondang.

04:05.620 --> 04:07.414
Marrying well is one of your duties.

04:08.373 --> 04:10.959
-Okay.
-Take what I say seriously.

04:11.585 --> 04:13.044
Everyone's watching you.

04:13.128 --> 04:14.337
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

04:14.421 --> 04:16.298
Don't forget
you must live for your dad, too.

04:17.591 --> 04:20.760
Only then will your grandpa
get over his anger in the afterlife.

04:21.386 --> 04:22.888
Do you know what I mean?

04:23.430 --> 04:25.307
I do. I'll do my best.

04:27.184 --> 04:28.185
Let's go inside.

04:28.810 --> 04:29.811
Sure.

05:06.890 --> 05:07.974
[door lock beeps open]

05:10.018 --> 05:11.853
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

05:35.043 --> 05:36.920
-[Sanghyeon] You're off to work early.
-[Meri exclaims]

05:37.462 --> 05:38.755
Good morning.

05:39.297 --> 05:42.300
Did your husband leave already?
His car isn't in the parking lot.

05:42.384 --> 05:43.385
[acknowledges]

05:44.553 --> 05:46.221
He worked late last night.

05:46.304 --> 05:48.431
He must be incredibly busy these days.

05:48.515 --> 05:49.599
[hums thoughtfully]

05:50.016 --> 05:51.852
Do you need a ride to the bus stop?

05:51.935 --> 05:53.144
No, it's fine.

05:53.228 --> 05:57.357
I love to contemplate on my way to work.

05:57.440 --> 05:58.567
[acknowledges]

05:59.276 --> 06:01.111
Why don't we have
breakfast together one day?

06:01.194 --> 06:03.989
You know the cafeteria here
serves breakfast, don't you?

06:04.656 --> 06:05.907
Yes, that would be nice.

06:05.991 --> 06:07.367
Okay, then.

06:07.450 --> 06:08.618
[Meri] Sure.

06:09.035 --> 06:10.036
Drive on.

06:10.120 --> 06:11.204
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

06:11.288 --> 06:12.289
[chuckles softly]

06:16.835 --> 06:17.919
[sighs]

06:19.296 --> 06:21.798
I should leave at the crack of dawn now.

06:24.634 --> 06:27.470
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

06:27.554 --> 06:28.597
EPISODE 5

06:28.680 --> 06:29.806
[chuckles] Welcome, Mr. Baek.

06:30.599 --> 06:32.934
Pleasure to meet you.
I'm Baek Sanghyeon of Beauté.

06:33.018 --> 06:35.312
Yes, thank you for making the trip over.

06:35.395 --> 06:36.688
This is our CFO.

06:36.771 --> 06:38.023
I'm Jang Hangu.

06:38.106 --> 06:39.524
I heard a lot about you from Mr. Lee.

06:39.608 --> 06:40.609
Oh, I see.

06:40.692 --> 06:42.277
-Let's sit down.
-Sure.

06:46.531 --> 06:49.159
Director Jang,
you're acquainted with Mr. Lee?

06:49.242 --> 06:50.994
Yes, we went to business school together.

06:51.077 --> 06:52.537
We play golf, too, sometimes.

06:52.621 --> 06:56.124
-[acknowledges]
-He meant to join us today,

06:56.207 --> 06:59.044
but he is currently hospitalized,
so I'm here on my own.

06:59.127 --> 07:01.796
Oh, my. Why is he in the hospital?

07:01.880 --> 07:03.423
It's nothing serious.

07:03.506 --> 07:05.216
He should watch his health.

07:05.300 --> 07:07.177
Your health is your biggest asset.

07:07.927 --> 07:12.098
I told him to get some well-earned rest.

07:12.599 --> 07:16.353
He asked me to send
some of our croquettes with Mr. Baek.

07:16.603 --> 07:18.313
-[hesitates]
-[all chuckling]

07:19.189 --> 07:22.192
We should pack him the best-tasting ones.

07:22.275 --> 07:23.693
[chuckles] Yes, I'll do that.

07:24.319 --> 07:25.737
-Have some tea.
-Yes, thanks.

07:27.572 --> 07:29.491
[Kim Wooju] A VVIP package?

07:29.949 --> 07:34.829
Yes, Beauté Department Store will gift
our hangwa set to their VVIP customers

07:34.913 --> 07:36.748
to celebrate their anniversary.

07:36.831 --> 07:38.917
-Beauté Department Store?
-Yes.

07:40.168 --> 07:41.252
[phone vibrates]

07:44.214 --> 07:46.424
[Meri] I'd like to come
and get the wallet.

07:46.508 --> 07:47.884
Are you free?

07:47.967 --> 07:49.803
[Kim Wooju] Yes,
call me when you get here.

07:49.886 --> 07:50.929
[telephone ringing]

07:52.389 --> 07:53.682
Hello, Kim Wooju speaking.

07:54.140 --> 07:55.141
[line disconnects]

07:55.225 --> 07:56.726
I told Mr. Kim to come over.

07:57.477 --> 08:01.272
You might as well meet the Head
of Marketing you'll be working with.

08:01.356 --> 08:03.066
Sure, that's fine with me.

08:06.444 --> 08:08.196
Good morning. Go on inside.

08:08.279 --> 08:13.201
I heard someone
from the Beauté Department Store was here.

08:13.284 --> 08:15.286
Yes, Managing Director Baek Sanghyeon.

08:15.370 --> 08:16.996
[stutters] Who? Baek Sanghyeon?

08:17.080 --> 08:18.373
Yes.

08:18.456 --> 08:19.916
[♪ gripping dramatic music playing]

08:20.417 --> 08:21.501
No, wait.

08:21.876 --> 08:22.919
[hesitates]

08:23.670 --> 08:26.548
I need to take an urgent bathroom break.

08:26.631 --> 08:28.633
-Pardon?
-[grunts, farts]

08:28.717 --> 08:29.801
[groans]

08:29.968 --> 08:31.302
Oh, I see.

08:31.386 --> 08:33.346
-Go ahead.
-Thanks. [groaning]

08:33.430 --> 08:35.098
CEO
KO PHILNYUN

08:36.599 --> 08:37.600
[farts, grunts]

08:49.195 --> 08:50.697
Should I leave work early?

08:51.614 --> 08:53.074
[sighs] No, it's too random.

08:54.159 --> 08:57.287
Oh, a business meeting elsewhere.
Don't I have one of those?

08:57.370 --> 08:58.788
JULY

09:00.373 --> 09:01.374
SECRETARY'S OFFICE

09:01.458 --> 09:02.459
[gasps]

09:03.043 --> 09:04.085
[phone vibrating]

09:08.256 --> 09:09.257
Yes, hello?

09:10.091 --> 09:14.596
Oh, well, you see,
I'm having some bathroom issues.

09:14.679 --> 09:15.847
I can't come right away.

09:15.930 --> 09:19.225
Right, could you talk to Mr. Jang for me?

09:20.351 --> 09:21.352
Thank you.

09:22.854 --> 09:23.855
[line disconnects]

09:25.607 --> 09:26.608
[sighs deeply]

09:26.691 --> 09:29.027
Everyone will call me a pooper now.

09:29.694 --> 09:30.862
[♪ whimsical sting]

09:37.535 --> 09:38.536
[Hangu] Mr. Kim?

09:38.912 --> 09:40.497
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

09:41.956 --> 09:42.957
Mr. Jang.

09:47.545 --> 09:50.131
I'm glad you two get to meet.

09:50.215 --> 09:52.634
This is Kim Wooju, our Head of Marketing.

09:52.717 --> 09:55.345
This is Beauté Department Store's
Managing Director Baek.

09:56.262 --> 09:57.305
[mumbles]

09:58.515 --> 09:59.557
Hello.

10:00.100 --> 10:01.434
It's nice to meet you.

10:03.353 --> 10:04.813
Nice to meet you, too.

10:04.896 --> 10:06.022
I'm Baek Sanghyeon.

10:13.029 --> 10:14.114
[chuckles]

10:15.156 --> 10:17.158
[Hangu] This is great. [chuckles softly]

10:19.452 --> 10:21.663
-I'll see you again soon.
-Drive back safely.

10:22.664 --> 10:24.499
-See him off.
-Sure thing.

10:27.627 --> 10:28.628
[elevator button beeps]

10:35.635 --> 10:37.262
So, this is where you work.

10:38.054 --> 10:39.097
Well, yes.

10:40.390 --> 10:43.143
I pretended not to know you
in case you felt uncomfortable.

10:44.519 --> 10:45.854
Separating work from life

10:45.937 --> 10:48.523
is very important
when dealing with business partners.

10:49.732 --> 10:52.402
Letting mistakes slide
because you're acquaintances?

10:52.485 --> 10:59.325
I don't care much for personal connections
forged in school or social circles.

10:59.784 --> 11:02.996
Of course. Not in this day and age.

11:03.079 --> 11:04.539
I agree with you completely.

11:04.622 --> 11:06.875
[chuckles softly]
Thank you for understanding.

11:06.958 --> 11:07.959
[acknowledges]

11:10.795 --> 11:12.672
Since we're on the topic,

11:12.755 --> 11:15.341
-could I ask for a favor?
-I know.

11:16.217 --> 11:18.303
You want me to keep your secret, right?

11:20.054 --> 11:22.640
[Sanghyeon] The winners used false names?

11:22.724 --> 11:25.768
The couple was terrified
that the creditors would come after them.

11:25.852 --> 11:27.562
They begged me to keep it a secret.

11:28.521 --> 11:32.108
They insisted we use false names
in the articles we release.

11:32.984 --> 11:35.069
Yes, that's right.

11:35.153 --> 11:36.279
I'm in debt,

11:37.155 --> 11:41.117
so I won't have much left
even if I were to sell the unit.

11:41.743 --> 11:43.411
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

11:44.621 --> 11:48.458
You look pretty good
for someone who worked late last night.

11:50.877 --> 11:52.295
I worked late?

11:52.378 --> 11:53.546
[elevator dings]

11:55.381 --> 11:56.883
[♪ dramatic sting]

11:56.966 --> 11:57.967
Hey, Mr. Ki...

11:59.928 --> 12:01.012
Honey.

12:02.055 --> 12:03.306
Oh, honey.

12:07.018 --> 12:08.728
What are you doing here, Mr. Baek?

12:09.354 --> 12:10.980
[clears throat] He's here for work.

12:11.064 --> 12:12.190
-For work?
-Yes.

12:12.732 --> 12:14.859
Do you work here, too, Ms. Yoo?

12:14.943 --> 12:17.403
-I'm not employed here--
-Her wallet.

12:18.196 --> 12:20.740
-She's here for her wallet.
-Oh, yes.

12:20.823 --> 12:24.369
He took my wallet with him to work.
This is my wallet.

12:24.452 --> 12:26.162
-[chuckles softly]
-[exclaims in realization]

12:26.246 --> 12:28.456
When a married couple lives together,

12:28.539 --> 12:30.750
-their belongings get mixed up.
-[Meri] Yes.

12:31.334 --> 12:33.336
-Hers is mine, and mine's hers.
-Right.

12:33.920 --> 12:37.173
I left in a hurry early this morning
and wasn't paying attention.

12:37.799 --> 12:39.884
-This morning--
-Yesterday morning.

12:40.343 --> 12:43.346
Sweetie, you worked late last night.

12:44.430 --> 12:46.182
You've been so busy
that yesterday and today

12:46.266 --> 12:48.726
-just blur together, right?
-Oh, it was yesterday.

12:49.310 --> 12:52.146
I've been so scatterbrained these days.

12:52.230 --> 12:53.856
He's pretty out of it.

12:53.940 --> 12:55.400
[Kim Wooju chuckles nervously]

12:58.278 --> 12:59.487
I'll go ahead, then.

12:59.988 --> 13:01.948
-Yes, get back safely.
-Goodbye.

13:06.869 --> 13:07.870
[sighs]

13:07.954 --> 13:08.955
[sighs in exasperation]

13:09.038 --> 13:11.541
-Do you think that went okay?
-Yes.

13:13.126 --> 13:14.252
[exhales]

13:14.335 --> 13:17.380
What? You're working
with Managing Director Baek?

13:17.463 --> 13:21.009
I won't deal with him directly,
but we must be as careful as possible.

13:21.092 --> 13:22.135
[sighs nervously]

13:23.094 --> 13:26.556
We met this morning,
and he asked about you.

13:26.639 --> 13:28.933
I said you worked late last night.

13:29.767 --> 13:30.768
I worked late?

13:31.769 --> 13:34.897
You look pretty good
for someone who worked late last night.

13:34.981 --> 13:36.107
[exclaims in realization]

13:36.691 --> 13:40.320
You should've told me about that.
I need time to plan a defense.

13:40.403 --> 13:42.113
I didn't think you'd meet like this.

13:42.196 --> 13:44.824
From now on,
call right away if you see Mr. Baek.

13:45.491 --> 13:49.162
No, call me three times a day,
no exceptions.

13:49.245 --> 13:50.455
At breakfast, lunch, and dinner.

13:50.913 --> 13:52.123
-Three times a day?
-Yes.

13:52.623 --> 13:55.626
We must share our day
to prevent messing up.

13:55.710 --> 13:57.587
[chuckles] Do we have to go that far?

13:57.670 --> 14:00.923
That naive mindset
caused what just happened.

14:01.007 --> 14:03.259
And, well...

14:04.010 --> 14:07.221
Newlyweds call each other
a dozen times a day.

14:07.764 --> 14:10.725
We're not actual newlyweds.

14:12.727 --> 14:15.730
-Aren't you too into this?
-"Too into this?"

14:15.813 --> 14:16.856
[♪ feel-good music playing]

14:16.939 --> 14:19.567
[stutters] Do you think
I'm doing this for me?

14:19.650 --> 14:23.071
I'm not. I just want to prevent risk.

14:23.613 --> 14:25.281
I'm a busy man, you know.

14:25.364 --> 14:26.574
I know you are.

14:26.657 --> 14:28.076
At breakfast, lunch, and dinner.

14:28.159 --> 14:29.827
Oh, and one more time before bed.

14:29.911 --> 14:31.037
Four times a day.

14:31.120 --> 14:32.246
And we'll talk before bed.

14:32.330 --> 14:33.581
-Okay.
-[phone vibrates]

14:36.459 --> 14:39.337
[Songhee] Where are you, Ms. Yoo?
The meeting's about to start.

14:39.420 --> 14:41.464
The meeting's about to start.

14:41.547 --> 14:42.715
I'll go upstairs first.

14:42.799 --> 14:44.550
You can come in a bit later.

14:44.634 --> 14:46.469
It would look weird
if we came in together.

14:46.552 --> 14:47.553
Yes, right.

14:52.475 --> 14:53.518
[chuckles softly]

14:53.976 --> 14:54.977
[clears throat]

15:00.608 --> 15:01.859
-[hums in satisfaction]
-[meowing]

15:01.943 --> 15:03.277
The laver is good. Where is it from?

15:03.361 --> 15:05.780
Hey, I seasoned it myself.

15:05.863 --> 15:07.657
With a mix of perilla oil and sesame oil.

15:07.740 --> 15:09.700
I followed a famous cook's recipe
just to feed you.

15:09.784 --> 15:10.827
[both chuckle]

15:10.910 --> 15:11.911
-Did you?
-Yes.

15:12.286 --> 15:13.371
[meowing]

15:15.706 --> 15:18.084
Did you meet Jenny's parents?

15:20.128 --> 15:21.337
Why would I meet them?

15:21.420 --> 15:24.465
Why didn't you pay them a visit
while you were in Hong Kong?

15:24.549 --> 15:25.716
[mouthing] Hurry over here.

15:26.300 --> 15:27.760
-[clears throat]
-[Elizabeth meowing]

15:27.844 --> 15:28.845
Hey!

15:29.846 --> 15:32.598
Introduce her to us quickly
before she changes her mind.

15:33.975 --> 15:36.352
There's an opening on the main road
where the ice cream shop was.

15:36.811 --> 15:38.521
I need to put down a deposit soon.

15:40.314 --> 15:41.315
[cutlery clatters on plate]

15:41.399 --> 15:43.985
Do you want to marry me off
so you can open your own store?

15:44.068 --> 15:45.278
Exactly.

15:45.361 --> 15:47.905
Let's benefit
from my handsome brother for once.

15:47.989 --> 15:50.449
Gosh! Forget it!

15:50.533 --> 15:51.534
[meows]

15:52.201 --> 15:54.912
Hey, where are you going?
You didn't finish your food.

15:54.996 --> 15:56.080
Hey!

15:59.041 --> 16:01.252
They expect so much from me.

16:02.128 --> 16:03.337
What should I tell them?

16:05.631 --> 16:06.757
No, wait.

16:06.841 --> 16:08.176
[♪ jazz music playing over speakers]

16:08.259 --> 16:09.302
You mean

16:09.635 --> 16:11.762
you and the guy in Room 3613

16:12.513 --> 16:14.348
-are getting married?
-Yes.

16:14.807 --> 16:16.726
Our families made a pact
when we were young.

16:16.809 --> 16:19.103
[loudly] Why are you telling me that now?
I thought we...

16:21.063 --> 16:22.106
[mumbles]

16:24.692 --> 16:26.694
You never said you had a fiancé.

16:26.777 --> 16:28.112
You never asked.

16:28.404 --> 16:29.405
[sighs in disbelief]

16:31.490 --> 16:32.658
[chuckles softly]

16:33.075 --> 16:35.536
Baby, are you jealous?

16:37.788 --> 16:38.998
Don't worry.

16:39.081 --> 16:41.292
My fiancé goes abroad a lot for work.

16:41.375 --> 16:44.420
-I'll have time for you when he's gone.
-Jenny.

16:44.503 --> 16:46.214
I gave up everything for you.

16:46.631 --> 16:48.132
How can you do this to me?

16:48.216 --> 16:51.427
-What do you want me to do?
-You must choose!

16:52.762 --> 16:55.097
You can never have two husbands.

16:56.682 --> 16:57.850
It's him or me.

16:59.101 --> 17:00.228
Who do you choose?

17:01.646 --> 17:02.939
Then...

17:05.816 --> 17:07.318
-[buzzer sounds]
-You're out.

17:09.528 --> 17:11.030
Drink your tea. It's nice.

17:11.113 --> 17:12.323
[♪ dramatic sting]

17:12.406 --> 17:13.574
[sighs wearily]

17:21.207 --> 17:22.667
[Wooju] What should I do with Elizabeth?

17:24.377 --> 17:26.170
[Jenny] I'm busy planning my wedding.

17:26.254 --> 17:27.380
Leave her with my relative.

17:27.463 --> 17:29.131
I'll text you the address.

17:30.925 --> 17:32.885
[♪ gentle pop music playing]

17:33.553 --> 17:34.679
[breath trembling]

17:35.888 --> 17:37.723
EVERYTHING I WANT TO DO WITH YOU

17:38.099 --> 17:39.225
-[Wooju] Meri.
-Yes?

17:40.601 --> 17:41.769
Why do you like me?

17:43.187 --> 17:44.397
Because you're good-looking.

17:44.814 --> 17:46.148
[Wooju chuckles]

17:46.232 --> 17:47.233
You're so cute.

18:01.122 --> 18:02.456
To Meri...

18:04.250 --> 18:05.835
I was her one and only.

18:06.877 --> 18:08.129
I'm sorry, Meri.

18:11.340 --> 18:13.050
[die-cut machine clicks rhythmically]

18:14.218 --> 18:15.428
[die-cut machine beeping]

18:22.059 --> 18:25.187
It's for food packaging,
so it should be moisture-proof,

18:25.605 --> 18:29.275
but it won't look or feel fancy
if the paper's too stiff.

18:32.862 --> 18:35.865
What's this? "Pergraphics?"

18:35.948 --> 18:39.076
We imported that from Austria
to test it out.

18:41.203 --> 18:42.622
It's nice and smooth.

18:43.080 --> 18:44.498
-It's nice, isn't it?
-It is.

18:44.582 --> 18:47.835
N Design ordered some boxes
to send out a cosmetics gift set,

18:47.918 --> 18:49.170
and people are loving it.

18:49.253 --> 18:51.047
Do you have any left?

18:51.130 --> 18:52.173
How many do you need?

18:52.256 --> 18:55.676
About 500 in the size
of the beef jerky sets I got last time.

18:56.552 --> 18:58.095
Let me have a look.

19:01.015 --> 19:02.266
[phone vibrating]

19:03.434 --> 19:04.602
PARK GYEONGHWA

19:05.436 --> 19:08.022
Hey, Gyeonghwa. Are you done?

19:08.105 --> 19:09.148
[knock at door]

19:09.774 --> 19:11.859
My goodness. Are you next? Come on in.

19:11.942 --> 19:14.320
-Hello.
-Take a seat.

19:15.821 --> 19:18.074
[Gyeonghwa] Man, these defense seminars
really bored me.

19:18.157 --> 19:19.784
I'd rather die, you know?

19:19.867 --> 19:21.243
Why didn't you just die, then?

19:21.327 --> 19:22.620
How could you say that?

19:22.703 --> 19:23.704
[chuckles softly]

19:23.788 --> 19:24.789
Pyongyang naengmyeon?

19:24.872 --> 19:26.207
-Minus the cucumber.
-Yes.

19:26.290 --> 19:27.750
Auntie.

19:28.709 --> 19:29.919
Yes?

19:30.002 --> 19:32.505
I'm really sorry, ladies.

19:32.588 --> 19:35.132
It's the lunchtime rush.
Can I let someone join you?

19:35.341 --> 19:38.678
[chuckles] You over there.
Come sit over here.

19:38.761 --> 19:40.012
[chuckles]

19:46.018 --> 19:47.019
Hey.

19:47.103 --> 19:48.437
[♪ whimsical sting]

19:54.318 --> 19:55.945
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

20:00.741 --> 20:03.369
I'm Meri's friend, Park Gyeonghwa.

20:03.452 --> 20:06.205
Oh, I heard a lot about you.

20:06.288 --> 20:07.581
Her army friend.

20:08.290 --> 20:09.917
When did you tell him about me?

20:10.626 --> 20:11.711
[both chuckle softly]

20:12.128 --> 20:13.254
Talk normally.

20:13.838 --> 20:15.172
-Was that weird?
-Yes.

20:15.256 --> 20:16.340
[mumbles, clears throat]

20:17.883 --> 20:20.928
-[clears throat]
-How do you know of this place?

20:21.011 --> 20:22.972
It's a hidden gem
only a few people know about.

20:24.098 --> 20:28.102
My boss from when I worked in New York
knew this place.

20:28.978 --> 20:32.022
He loved Pyongyang naengmyeon
and often mentioned this place.

20:32.523 --> 20:34.692
-[Gyeonghwa] Eat up.
-Yes, thanks. [chuckles]

20:35.192 --> 20:36.402
[inhales deeply]

20:41.991 --> 20:43.159
[Gyeonghwa slurping]

20:45.578 --> 20:47.288
[continues slurping, stops]

20:49.248 --> 20:51.625
Your smile. It reminds me of him.

20:52.293 --> 20:54.545
His eyes were just as pretty.

20:56.088 --> 20:58.382
-Who...
-My first love.

20:58.799 --> 20:59.800
[Kim Wooju exclaims]

21:00.301 --> 21:01.844
[chuckles] I see.

21:03.637 --> 21:05.139
[♪ enthralling orchestral music playing]

21:05.222 --> 21:06.515
[Kim Wooju slurping]

21:06.974 --> 21:08.058
[Gyeonghwa] His skull...

21:08.476 --> 21:12.313
His head shape was petite and pretty,
just like yours.

21:12.396 --> 21:14.523
It looked so nice when shaved.

21:14.607 --> 21:16.108
[Meri] Darn you. Stop it.

21:17.777 --> 21:21.739
-Her first love became a Buddhist monk.
-[exclaims quizzically]

21:21.822 --> 21:23.908
He shaved his head to move into a temple,

21:23.991 --> 21:26.243
and I cut mine short to join the army.

21:26.327 --> 21:28.412
We shared a farewell drink right here.

21:28.496 --> 21:29.997
With a small plate of boiled pork.

21:30.080 --> 21:31.290
[exclaims in realization]

21:31.957 --> 21:33.250
That must've broken your heart.

21:33.334 --> 21:35.669
Such is life. It can get salty with tears.

21:38.005 --> 21:39.215
Oh, sure.

21:41.008 --> 21:44.762
First love is like an installment
savings plan that's meant to be canceled.

21:44.845 --> 21:47.473
Pretend he's out there doing just fine.

21:47.556 --> 21:49.767
You can say that
about your boy, Occipital.

21:50.434 --> 21:54.438
There's a boy we call Occipital.
Her elementary school first love.

21:54.772 --> 21:55.856
[acknowledges]

21:56.232 --> 21:57.566
Myungsik...

21:58.234 --> 21:59.235
Who's Myungsik?

21:59.318 --> 22:01.403
-The same guy.
-[Gyeonghwa] Oh, really?

22:01.487 --> 22:04.365
Anyway, she gave him her favorite toy,

22:04.448 --> 22:06.784
but he rejected her without a thank-you.

22:07.451 --> 22:08.494
-A toy?
-Yes.

22:08.577 --> 22:12.456
She gave it to him out of pity
because he was shaking after a car crash.

22:12.540 --> 22:16.043
Ever since, she's been giving,
and everyone takes advantage of her.

22:16.126 --> 22:18.003
-You got off on the wrong foot.
-[exclaims]

22:18.587 --> 22:21.298
You talk too much.
Will you eat until tomorrow?

22:21.382 --> 22:22.383
Sorry.

22:22.466 --> 22:24.677
So, that's why...

22:24.760 --> 22:27.471
He's called Occipital
because he had a cute head.

22:28.389 --> 22:30.015
It was very spherical.

22:30.558 --> 22:33.018
The kind that makes you want to touch it.

22:33.936 --> 22:35.688
[♪ dreamy pop music playing]

22:35.771 --> 22:36.939
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

22:40.109 --> 22:42.027
Did you ever see him since then?

22:42.111 --> 22:44.905
Yeosu's pretty small.
You'd have crossed paths once.

22:45.364 --> 22:46.740
He wasn't from there, I guess.

22:46.824 --> 22:47.825
No?

22:48.909 --> 22:50.286
You don't remember him at all?

22:51.078 --> 22:52.329
No.

22:52.413 --> 22:54.164
We met really briefly.

22:56.125 --> 22:59.086
If we were to meet again,
I'd recognize him right away.

23:00.838 --> 23:02.673
He was so good-looking.

23:04.717 --> 23:06.260
He was totally my type.

23:07.511 --> 23:10.014
I bet he grew up to be just as handsome.

23:26.947 --> 23:28.490
[Gyeonghwa] This place doesn't disappoint.

23:29.867 --> 23:31.994
-Thanks for the meal.
-Thanks for paying.

23:32.077 --> 23:34.121
I'll treat you
to kaoliang liquor next time.

23:34.204 --> 23:35.998
I know a place with fine five-spice pork.

23:36.081 --> 23:37.291
Sounds good.

23:37.374 --> 23:39.585
And this is...

23:41.045 --> 23:42.796
-[Kim Wooju] What's this?
-It's a souvenir I got

23:42.880 --> 23:44.548
from today's defense seminar.

23:44.632 --> 23:46.926
It's an aftershave for men.

23:47.009 --> 23:49.386
But I don't have a man to give it to.
[giggles]

23:49.470 --> 23:51.805
[chuckles] Thanks a lot.

23:52.514 --> 23:53.849
[exclaims]

23:53.933 --> 23:56.143
-What's this?
-Oh, that?

23:56.685 --> 23:57.853
It's for you.

23:57.937 --> 24:00.522
-Am I your trash can?
-Take it already.

24:07.071 --> 24:08.822
Don't sit on that one.

24:09.823 --> 24:11.325
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

24:11.408 --> 24:12.576
[Meri grunts]

24:16.205 --> 24:17.456
[acknowledges, chuckles softly]

24:17.539 --> 24:19.083
-Okay.
-[both chuckle]

24:26.548 --> 24:28.384
The taxi's here. You should get in.

24:28.467 --> 24:30.678
-We'll go somewhere for tea.
-Okay, then.

24:33.305 --> 24:35.724
-Bye, I'll be in touch.
-Okay.

24:36.183 --> 24:37.184
[hesitates]

24:44.191 --> 24:46.068
[Gyeonghwa] What a pity
we must let him go.

24:46.652 --> 24:48.570
Why would you be in touch with him?

24:48.654 --> 24:50.864
-You go too far.
-What's wrong with that?

24:53.325 --> 24:56.829
There's a boy we call Occipital.
Her elementary school first love.

24:56.912 --> 24:58.914
He was so good-looking.

25:00.082 --> 25:01.667
He was totally my type.

25:08.716 --> 25:11.301
I bet he grew up to be just as handsome.

25:23.022 --> 25:25.315
You're fine, as you always were.

25:26.275 --> 25:28.944
-My neck and shoulders still feel stiff.
-[neck cracking]

25:29.028 --> 25:30.863
And my eyes are dry.

25:30.946 --> 25:32.823
I request a brain MRI.

25:34.324 --> 25:35.451
[Jingyeong sighs]

25:36.910 --> 25:39.413
That's because you play games all day.

25:40.080 --> 25:41.623
You have a tech neck and poor eyesight.

25:42.916 --> 25:45.836
My stomach burns, and I have indigestion.

25:45.919 --> 25:47.296
I request a gastroscopy.

25:47.379 --> 25:49.089
[snaps fingers] Under sedation.

25:49.173 --> 25:50.174
[chuckles softly]

25:52.718 --> 25:54.303
-[squelch]
-[screams]

25:54.636 --> 25:55.804
[groans softly]

25:55.888 --> 25:56.889
You're fine.

25:56.972 --> 25:58.015
That was meant to hurt.

25:58.098 --> 25:59.600
Why did you do that, then?

26:00.851 --> 26:01.852
[scoffs]

26:02.895 --> 26:03.896
Doctor.

26:03.979 --> 26:05.522
Your patient says he's in pain.

26:06.231 --> 26:07.316
[sighs]

26:12.196 --> 26:13.238
[♪ whimsical music playing]

26:13.322 --> 26:15.449
[Jingyeong] Gosh, you snack a lot.

26:15.532 --> 26:18.243
Dried fishcake, dried squid, beef jerky.

26:18.327 --> 26:19.536
[scoffs softly]

26:19.703 --> 26:21.830
You eat stuff that's bad for you
late at night.

26:21.914 --> 26:23.540
It would give anyone indigestion.

26:27.753 --> 26:28.754
[Jingyeong gasps]

26:29.129 --> 26:30.130
[chuckles]

26:30.672 --> 26:32.925
And in this sacred hospital room...

26:35.219 --> 26:37.012
you've even been drinking?

26:37.096 --> 26:39.348
I haven't been able to sleep.

26:39.431 --> 26:40.933
That's my sleeping aid.

26:41.016 --> 26:42.017
Do you like wine?

26:43.435 --> 26:45.854
-Confiscate this from now on.
-Yes, Doctor.

26:48.941 --> 26:50.400
You're a terrible patient,

26:51.777 --> 26:55.030
but you're just as bad
for getting him whatever he wants.

26:55.906 --> 26:57.908
You can go home before this weekend.

27:00.327 --> 27:01.328
Doctor.

27:03.038 --> 27:04.581
I request an extended stay.

27:04.665 --> 27:08.127
The patient needs to rest
until the end of the month.

27:08.210 --> 27:09.586
This isn't a hotel.

27:10.129 --> 27:13.382
He has been here for over a week,
and it's time he went home.

27:13.757 --> 27:15.551
We're short on beds as it is.

27:16.510 --> 27:18.595
I'll have you discharged within the week.

27:21.890 --> 27:23.642
I made myself very clear.

27:28.438 --> 27:30.357
[Sungwoo] Hey, leave it.

27:32.025 --> 27:33.402
She's a total nutcase.

27:33.485 --> 27:35.904
She's the hospital director's daughter,
and she never backs down.

27:37.406 --> 27:39.366
Go talk to the director in person.

27:40.576 --> 27:41.785
[sighs]

27:44.913 --> 27:47.666
[sighs] I can't stand jerks
who pretend to be ill.

27:47.749 --> 27:49.418
[exclaims] I wish he'd just disappear.

27:50.419 --> 27:53.380
No more vertical wrinkles.
Smile, Yoon Jingyeong.

27:53.463 --> 27:55.173
Relax your facial muscles.

27:56.842 --> 27:58.051
[exhales]

27:58.135 --> 27:59.344
[doctor] Hey, Yoon Jingyeong!

28:00.888 --> 28:02.014
[panting]

28:02.097 --> 28:04.850
Jingyeong, I need a favor.

28:04.933 --> 28:07.519
-I'm on night watch today--
-Oh, my dear senior doctor.

28:07.603 --> 28:10.147
I would pretend to die
if you told me to die.

28:10.981 --> 28:12.608
But I can't swap with you today.

28:12.691 --> 28:15.777
The most important appointment
of my life is today.

28:16.737 --> 28:18.280
[inhales deeply] I'm really sorry.

28:19.406 --> 28:21.742
Hey, Jingyeong. Yoon Jingyeong!

28:22.326 --> 28:23.327
Sorry!

28:25.662 --> 28:27.164
[♪ live jazz music playing]

28:59.488 --> 29:00.489
Wooju.

29:00.572 --> 29:01.573
Hey.

29:01.657 --> 29:02.950
[gasps in awe]

29:04.201 --> 29:05.619
Did you have a blind date today?

29:05.702 --> 29:07.037
You're all dressed up.

29:07.120 --> 29:10.457
[chuckles] I didn't have a blind date.
I just dressed for the location.

29:11.041 --> 29:14.336
Why did you book such a nice place?
It's too much pressure.

29:14.419 --> 29:15.879
My grandma booked the table.

29:15.963 --> 29:17.756
She told me to treat you
to something nice.

29:18.256 --> 29:21.218
You made a house call to check on her
while your father was away?

29:21.301 --> 29:22.803
[exclaims quizzically]

29:22.886 --> 29:25.597
-Your grandmother made the reservation?
-Yes.

29:25.681 --> 29:26.848
[chuckles softly]

29:27.849 --> 29:29.393
I like the atmosphere.

29:29.768 --> 29:30.769
[chuckles softly]

29:31.687 --> 29:32.896
What do you want to eat?

29:34.898 --> 29:36.358
[♪ jazz music continues]

29:43.073 --> 29:45.659
When the idol trainee dumped you,

29:46.243 --> 29:49.997
you wailed so hard
that you got snot and tears all over me.

29:50.622 --> 29:52.290
It was an expensive shirt, too.

29:52.708 --> 29:55.252
We only dated for less than a month.

29:56.503 --> 29:57.963
I was young and immature.

29:58.046 --> 30:00.090
You weren't young. You were 23.

30:01.299 --> 30:03.719
-The ice hockey player after that--
-That guy...

30:04.636 --> 30:05.637
I dumped him, okay?

30:05.721 --> 30:06.888
Whatever.

30:06.972 --> 30:09.307
You came all the way to the US to cry.

30:09.391 --> 30:12.477
I spent so much time with you
that I ruined my finals.

30:12.561 --> 30:15.188
How about we cover up
each other's embarrassing past?

30:15.689 --> 30:17.941
I know all about your ex
and the ex before that.

30:18.025 --> 30:21.153
They came to me to complain
whenever you made them angry.

30:21.236 --> 30:23.405
-What did they say?
-Why ask when you know?

30:24.239 --> 30:25.824
"Kim Wooju, that son of a b****."

30:25.907 --> 30:28.160
"The selfish punk
who cares only about himself."

30:28.243 --> 30:29.327
"He's total scum."

30:29.870 --> 30:33.623
Anyway, you're no longer welcome
in the blind date market.

30:34.166 --> 30:35.417
Your grandmother knows that, too.

30:35.500 --> 30:37.461
That's why she won't tell you
to go on blind dates.

30:37.711 --> 30:40.672
[sighs] That's not good at all.
What should I do now?

30:41.423 --> 30:43.759
So, I gave it some thought.

30:44.301 --> 30:46.762
Who could possibly save you, Wooju?

30:47.929 --> 30:49.598
There's no need to look very far.

30:50.098 --> 30:52.851
The person could be under your nose.

31:00.400 --> 31:04.404
This could be a bit flustering for you,

31:05.155 --> 31:06.281
but listen carefully.

31:07.866 --> 31:09.659
Actually, I...

31:09.743 --> 31:11.286
-[♪ music stops]
-[all applauding, cheering]

31:30.639 --> 31:32.432
-Jingyeong.
-Yes?

31:32.849 --> 31:34.267
Were you...

31:36.228 --> 31:37.813
looking at the back of my head?

31:38.563 --> 31:39.564
What?

31:40.690 --> 31:42.275
[hesitates] Why do you ask?

31:42.776 --> 31:45.403
Someone said
the back of my head looked pretty.

31:45.862 --> 31:47.697
-Who? A woman?
-Yes.

31:48.615 --> 31:49.616
Well... [chuckles softly]

31:50.200 --> 31:51.785
She saw it a long time ago,

31:52.536 --> 31:53.745
but she still remembered it.

31:54.663 --> 31:55.664
[chuckles softly]

31:56.790 --> 31:58.542
Is that why you're in a good mood?

31:58.625 --> 32:00.252
Because someone praised your head shape?

32:00.335 --> 32:01.753
-I'm not in a good mood.
-You are.

32:02.212 --> 32:04.047
You're a bit more upbeat than usual.

32:05.132 --> 32:06.800
Did you meet your first love or something?

32:13.098 --> 32:14.224
You should become a psychic.

32:15.517 --> 32:16.977
-You actually met her?
-Yes.

32:17.644 --> 32:18.645
Actually,

32:19.563 --> 32:21.648
I met the owner of the key ring.

32:21.731 --> 32:23.650
What? She's alive?

32:24.401 --> 32:25.861
-Here in Korea?
-Yes.

32:25.944 --> 32:27.737
Where did you meet? Did she call?

32:29.072 --> 32:30.240
Not really.

32:33.952 --> 32:34.995
Do you remember Yoo Meri?

32:35.078 --> 32:36.079
Yoo Meri?

32:37.581 --> 32:38.582
The cactus girl?

32:41.835 --> 32:43.837
-It's her?
-[chuckles] Yes.

32:44.296 --> 32:45.714
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

32:45.797 --> 32:46.965
[exclaims in realization]

32:47.048 --> 32:49.176
Do you see the goosebumps?

32:49.801 --> 32:51.553
How did you figure it out?

32:52.137 --> 32:53.889
Does she also know who you are?

32:53.972 --> 32:56.266
No, she doesn't know yet.

32:56.349 --> 32:57.434
Only I do.

32:57.517 --> 32:58.768
[hums thoughtfully]

32:59.811 --> 33:01.271
That's really fascinating.

33:01.855 --> 33:02.939
It is.

33:03.023 --> 33:04.649
[breathes deeply]

33:04.733 --> 33:06.359
How did we meet again like this?

33:06.443 --> 33:09.237
I've always wanted to ask.

33:10.947 --> 33:12.365
Why didn't you look for her?

33:12.949 --> 33:14.618
You could've tried to find her.

33:16.203 --> 33:17.412
[acknowledges]

33:18.788 --> 33:20.332
I did look for her.

33:29.466 --> 33:31.676
[officer] Here's the address
the taxi driver put

33:31.760 --> 33:32.886
on his witness statement.

33:33.887 --> 33:35.889
I'm not sure if his family's still there.

33:36.723 --> 33:38.058
He died in an accident

33:38.141 --> 33:40.644
two weeks after the crash,
while coming in to give extra details.

33:46.691 --> 33:48.610
[Youngsook] I just don't get it.

33:48.693 --> 33:49.986
He talked to the police already.

33:50.070 --> 33:52.530
Why would he go back there
to talk to them again?

33:52.614 --> 33:54.783
He must've remembered something else.

33:54.866 --> 33:58.286
Would that family appreciate it
when the couple's already dead?

33:58.745 --> 34:01.706
Your dad ended up dead for being nosy.

34:01.790 --> 34:04.084
If only he hadn't gone
to the police station.

34:04.167 --> 34:05.293
[Youngsook sighs]

34:07.212 --> 34:08.380
PREMIUM ORANGE JUICE GIFT SET

34:24.271 --> 34:25.313
The truth is,

34:26.856 --> 34:28.275
I was too scared to see her.

34:31.444 --> 34:33.029
I was afraid she'd resent me.

34:34.447 --> 34:37.784
So, I don't know what to do next.

34:38.201 --> 34:40.328
Should I tell her or not?

34:40.412 --> 34:41.413
Don't tell her.

34:42.539 --> 34:44.165
[♪ melancholy music playing]

34:45.375 --> 34:46.376
Well...

34:47.669 --> 34:48.962
It would be best not to.

34:50.046 --> 34:54.259
She might think
her father died because of you.

34:59.764 --> 35:01.266
-Right?
-Yes.

35:01.850 --> 35:03.268
You should consider her feelings, too.

35:06.187 --> 35:07.188
Right.

35:28.209 --> 35:30.420
[inhales deeply] I'm sorry, sir.

35:31.630 --> 35:34.424
The interview was meant to explain
the social benefits of our raffle,

35:35.342 --> 35:37.260
but they wrote something else
without consulting us.

35:41.973 --> 35:42.974
It's fine.

35:43.516 --> 35:44.809
It was your chance.

35:45.268 --> 35:46.478
Since you are at it,

35:46.561 --> 35:48.897
why didn't you say you planned
the Beauté Palace event,

35:48.980 --> 35:51.608
and that you were behind
the 350% increase in sales?

35:53.151 --> 35:55.028
The Young Entrepreneur Award
I got last year...

35:56.071 --> 35:59.157
Why didn't you say you lobbied them
to give me your award, too?

35:59.240 --> 36:02.077
-I apologize.
-Why are you always apologizing?

36:03.870 --> 36:05.413
You work so hard, Sanghyeon.

36:06.164 --> 36:07.499
I should give you a bonus.

36:09.959 --> 36:10.960
Here.

36:12.212 --> 36:13.463
It's fine. Come closer.

36:14.297 --> 36:15.548
Come closer.

36:33.066 --> 36:34.109
Hey, Sanghyeon.

36:34.984 --> 36:36.319
You know what?

36:36.403 --> 36:39.572
No matter how hard you try,
you can't be me.

36:39.656 --> 36:41.157
[♪ tense melancholy music playing]

36:41.241 --> 36:42.742
Was it in middle school?

36:42.826 --> 36:45.245
We became friends
because you shielded me from the bullies.

36:46.705 --> 36:49.332
My dad sent you abroad to study
and made you Managing Director

36:49.416 --> 36:51.042
only because you were my friend.

36:51.126 --> 36:54.212
I get the impression
that you're mistaken sometimes.

36:54.754 --> 36:56.256
[chuckles]

36:56.339 --> 36:58.758
But then our pet dog, a shih tzu,

36:59.300 --> 37:02.595
thinks it's human
because it's fed and bathed.

37:07.934 --> 37:09.352
Spend that on some kibble.

37:12.147 --> 37:14.691
[inhales] I'll heed your warning.

37:20.739 --> 37:22.323
[♪ foreboding music playing]

37:44.012 --> 37:45.972
I should've just stayed to work late.

37:47.348 --> 37:49.309
What a waste of an expensive meal.

37:57.442 --> 37:58.526
[sighs wearily]

38:01.571 --> 38:02.614
Don't tell her.

38:02.697 --> 38:03.698
[♪ melancholy music playing]

38:03.782 --> 38:06.242
Well, it would be best not to.

38:06.826 --> 38:10.246
She might think
her father died because of you.

38:12.499 --> 38:13.500
Right.

38:15.210 --> 38:17.337
You're a coward, Jingyeong.

38:19.756 --> 38:23.593
Why did I say that,
knowing he would get hurt?

38:39.108 --> 38:40.819
[♪ playing "Chopsticks" on piano]

39:08.596 --> 39:10.098
[♪ "Chopsticks" continues]

39:27.407 --> 39:29.367
[♪ somber piano music playing]

39:53.641 --> 39:54.684
[sighs softly]

40:26.174 --> 40:27.717
[♪ piano music fades]

40:30.887 --> 40:31.971
[sighs softly]

40:33.222 --> 40:34.974
[wooden fish taps rhythmically]

40:38.144 --> 40:40.605
MAIN HALL

40:40.688 --> 40:42.357
[monk chanting prayers]

41:02.627 --> 41:03.962
[chanting continues]

41:15.014 --> 41:16.724
[wooden fish rhythmic taps continue]

41:21.354 --> 41:22.397
[sighing in exhaustion]

41:24.399 --> 41:27.110
Why does Mom have so much to say?

41:27.193 --> 41:28.820
Oh, I'm starving.

41:29.445 --> 41:31.155
What's for breakfast?

41:32.740 --> 41:34.117
It's obvious.

41:34.200 --> 41:35.994
The place across the road
we go to every year.

41:36.077 --> 41:37.912
Oh, that gukbap again?

41:38.788 --> 41:42.000
We can't have that every single year
just because Uncle used to like it.

41:42.083 --> 41:43.084
Don't you think

41:43.167 --> 41:46.337
it's time to assume he would be sick
of eating the same thing?

41:46.879 --> 41:48.423
-[scoffs]
-It would be nice

41:49.507 --> 41:51.175
to have pork cutlet sometimes.

41:51.259 --> 41:53.052
We can't have that for breakfast!

41:53.136 --> 41:55.054
I mean, Wooju likes it.

41:58.349 --> 42:00.476
It's his birthday today.

42:00.560 --> 42:01.561
What?

42:01.644 --> 42:04.856
You're his only aunt,
and you don't know that?

42:15.158 --> 42:17.910
He lived abroad most of the time.

42:18.411 --> 42:21.080
People forget stuff after a while.

42:22.457 --> 42:26.294
I feel really bad for the kid.

42:26.377 --> 42:30.673
He never got to celebrate his birthday
since his parents died on that day.

42:30.757 --> 42:33.009
He's lucky he wasn't kicked
out of the family.

42:33.092 --> 42:36.471
Why do you think my brother died?
It was because Wooju--

42:36.554 --> 42:38.973
-[Hangu] Honey.
-Yes, well, he was responsible for...

42:46.064 --> 42:47.899
Couldn't you have made a sound at least?

42:50.234 --> 42:54.197
Why is it so cold?
I'll go wait in the car.

42:54.280 --> 42:55.448
Where are you...

42:58.284 --> 42:59.911
Why do I feel so warm?

43:00.995 --> 43:01.996
Wait for me.

43:13.508 --> 43:15.176
[♪ melancholy music playing]

43:46.332 --> 43:47.333
Wooju.

43:47.416 --> 43:50.378
CONDOLENCES

43:50.461 --> 43:52.046
Talk to your dad

43:53.214 --> 43:55.383
if you have anything left to say.

43:57.677 --> 43:59.679
You won't see him ever again.

44:00.429 --> 44:02.557
Say what you want while you can.

44:03.182 --> 44:04.934
[crying, breath trembling]

44:09.605 --> 44:10.940
I'm sorry.

44:12.066 --> 44:13.151
[sighs softly]

44:18.906 --> 44:20.241
It was my fault.

44:28.207 --> 44:29.792
[Kim Wooju's dad]
Are you still upset, Wooju?

44:29.876 --> 44:32.295
It was my birthday present.

44:32.378 --> 44:34.297
Why did you give it to Eungsoo?

44:34.380 --> 44:36.132
It was mine.

44:36.215 --> 44:38.134
He wanted it.

44:38.843 --> 44:41.512
His whole family came
to wish you a happy birthday.

44:41.596 --> 44:42.889
Couldn't you give him that?

44:43.514 --> 44:47.310
I promise to buy you a new toy robot.

44:47.894 --> 44:49.270
-Let it go.
-No.

44:49.896 --> 44:53.107
Tell Eungsoo to give back what he took

44:53.191 --> 44:54.317
and buy him the robot.

44:55.651 --> 44:58.487
[whining] He always takes what's mine.

44:59.447 --> 45:01.908
-He's a mean pig.
-[Kim Wooju's dad disapproving]

45:01.991 --> 45:04.285
You can't talk like that
about your cousin.

45:04.368 --> 45:05.369
Take it back.

45:05.745 --> 45:07.788
Or Dad will get really angry.

45:07.872 --> 45:08.915
You won't take it back?

45:11.125 --> 45:14.170
You're a good boy, aren't you?
Do as your dad says.

45:15.630 --> 45:16.797
Come on.

45:16.881 --> 45:17.924
You won't take it back?

45:19.175 --> 45:20.259
[Kim Wooju's dad sighs]

45:21.344 --> 45:24.764
Then I won't buy you the toy robot.

45:27.433 --> 45:28.476
[gasps] Honey!

45:28.601 --> 45:29.936
[truck horn blaring]

45:31.103 --> 45:32.772
-[all scream]
-[horn blaring]

45:33.481 --> 45:34.815
[tires screeching]

45:47.495 --> 45:48.913
[♪ tense melancholy music playing]

45:48.996 --> 45:49.997
You mean...

45:53.000 --> 45:54.877
Your dad was in the accident...

45:57.296 --> 45:59.298
because he turned around to talk to you?

46:01.092 --> 46:02.218
[man] What was that?

46:02.802 --> 46:04.553
[breath trembling] Honey.

46:06.055 --> 46:08.849
I lost my son because of you, Wooju?

46:12.311 --> 46:13.896
[breathing heavily]

46:17.024 --> 46:18.109
[sighs]

46:29.912 --> 46:31.163
Okay.

46:32.581 --> 46:36.752
Make sure Mom eats something, Ms. Kim.

46:37.336 --> 46:38.337
Bye.

46:39.922 --> 46:40.965
[line disconnects]

46:42.133 --> 46:43.676
Grandma won't have breakfast?

46:43.759 --> 46:45.052
She doesn't feel well.

46:46.137 --> 46:47.763
She wouldn't feel like eating.

46:48.347 --> 46:50.266
Today at least,

46:50.349 --> 46:53.144
she'll think more of her dead son
than her dear grandson.

46:53.728 --> 46:54.937
[Eungsoo] True.

46:55.021 --> 46:59.025
Grandma didn't even glance at Wooju
during the whole service.

46:59.900 --> 47:02.278
Even when Grandpa
chased him away to the US,

47:02.361 --> 47:05.364
she only cared about Wooju, didn't she?
[scoffs]

47:05.448 --> 47:07.908
We must have breakfast without them.
What should we eat?

47:07.992 --> 47:10.453
How about malatang?
I found a famous place nearby.

47:10.536 --> 47:11.746
Let's have tofu hot pot.

47:12.788 --> 47:15.166
Why do you even ask? Don't ask me anymore.

47:15.249 --> 47:16.375
I won't.

47:17.376 --> 47:18.711
Are you okay with that?

47:18.794 --> 47:20.504
What? Oh, yes. It's fine.

47:25.134 --> 47:27.053
[♪ ominous music playing]

47:46.530 --> 47:48.991
I TOOK CARE OF IT

47:55.414 --> 47:57.583
I TOOK CARE OF IT

47:57.666 --> 47:59.126
[♪ ominous music crescendos]

48:11.722 --> 48:13.182
[♪ ominous sting]

48:13.265 --> 48:14.517
[rain pattering]

48:15.893 --> 48:17.228
[thunder rumbling]

48:38.666 --> 48:39.834
[exclaims quizzically]

48:40.584 --> 48:41.585
It flowered.

48:41.752 --> 48:42.753
[♪ whimsical music playing]

48:42.837 --> 48:44.046
Don't sit on that one.

48:44.630 --> 48:45.714
[Meri acknowledges]

48:46.298 --> 48:47.299
Okay. [chuckles]

49:02.690 --> 49:04.275
[thunder rumbling]

49:17.371 --> 49:18.998
-[Grandad] What was that?
-[Grandma] Honey.

49:20.207 --> 49:22.877
I lost my son because of you, Wooju?

49:22.960 --> 49:24.712
He's lucky he wasn't kicked
out of the family.

49:24.795 --> 49:27.506
Why do you think my brother died?

49:27.590 --> 49:29.091
-It was because Wooju--
-[Hangu] Honey.

49:33.387 --> 49:34.889
[♪ melancholy music playing]

49:41.604 --> 49:43.397
[breathing heavily]

49:51.238 --> 49:52.490
[continues breathing heavily]

49:56.994 --> 49:58.120
[vibrating]

50:09.840 --> 50:11.050
[panting]

50:12.676 --> 50:14.553
CEO YOO MERI

50:15.971 --> 50:19.225
[Meri] This cactus
must be a flowering kind.

50:22.144 --> 50:23.270
[vibrating]

50:23.354 --> 50:24.897
By the way, is it your birthday today?

50:24.980 --> 50:26.106
[panting]

50:32.112 --> 50:33.322
[rain pattering]

50:37.034 --> 50:38.869
TEAM LEADER KIM WOOJU
BIRTHDAY: TODAY

50:43.499 --> 50:45.209
I didn't know it was your birthday.

50:45.292 --> 50:47.211
What kind of cake do you like?

50:47.294 --> 50:48.712
I'll send you a cake coupon.

50:54.343 --> 50:55.594
It's not a bribe.

50:55.678 --> 50:58.138
-Allow me to congratulate you, at least.
-[panting]

51:00.766 --> 51:02.601
[Kim Wooju] Will you buy me a meal, then?

51:02.685 --> 51:03.686
I'm hungry.

51:04.353 --> 51:05.604
[♪ soft orchestral music playing]

51:05.688 --> 51:07.439
[Meri] How about a home-cooked meal?

51:07.523 --> 51:08.816
[breathing slows]

51:09.984 --> 51:11.193
[Meri gasps]

51:12.528 --> 51:14.905
Does it sound like I'm flirting?

51:20.286 --> 51:22.079
HOW ABOUT A HOME-COOKED MEAL?

51:37.428 --> 51:40.681
If we were to meet someone from work
at a restaurant on a weekend,

51:40.764 --> 51:42.641
-you might look--
-[Kim Wooju] I'm on my way.

51:44.143 --> 51:45.185
[exhales]

51:54.028 --> 51:55.237
Yes.

51:56.614 --> 51:57.698
It's a Sunday.

51:58.240 --> 52:00.451
Not many restaurants will be open.

52:00.534 --> 52:02.620
He bought me naengmyeon last time.

52:03.996 --> 52:05.539
He's always helping me out.

52:06.498 --> 52:11.253
I can cook him a meal. Why not?

52:14.089 --> 52:15.341
What do I have at home?

52:16.759 --> 52:18.135
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

52:33.400 --> 52:34.401
Rice.

53:09.311 --> 53:10.896
[Youngsook over phone] No, stop!

53:11.522 --> 53:14.149
Add just enough water
to cover the seaweed.

53:14.233 --> 53:16.360
You add water little by little

53:16.443 --> 53:18.570
-to keep the broth nice and rich.
-Is that it?

53:20.155 --> 53:21.949
-This much?
-Yes.

53:22.324 --> 53:23.575
Now let that simmer,

53:23.659 --> 53:25.869
and add the small octopus
at the last moment.

53:25.953 --> 53:27.955
-Or it'll go tough.
-Okay.

53:30.999 --> 53:34.086
Why are you suddenly cooking
seaweed soup with octopus?

53:35.546 --> 53:38.090
I decided to cook for myself for once.

53:38.173 --> 53:39.425
You, cook?

53:40.008 --> 53:43.679
Why don't you grill a yellow croaker,
and heat up some yukjeon as well?

53:43.762 --> 53:44.763
[chuckles]

53:44.847 --> 53:46.640
I'm thawing them already.

53:48.350 --> 53:49.560
[Youngsook gasps]

53:51.395 --> 53:52.855
Did you invite someone?

53:52.938 --> 53:53.939
[♪ feel-good music playing]

53:54.022 --> 53:56.024
Like who? No one's coming.

53:56.608 --> 53:57.860
I'm cooking for myself.

53:57.943 --> 54:00.028
You're going to eat all that on your own?

54:00.446 --> 54:01.447
Yes.

54:01.864 --> 54:04.074
I need to free up some freezer space.

54:04.158 --> 54:05.325
Of course, you do.

54:05.743 --> 54:08.495
If you're making the effort,

54:08.579 --> 54:11.290
why don't you bring out the pretty plates?

54:11.373 --> 54:14.126
The ones you bought
to use after the wedding.

54:14.209 --> 54:17.087
That's it. I'd forgotten about those.

54:20.883 --> 54:21.884
Why go that far

54:22.968 --> 54:24.303
when it's just me?

54:24.386 --> 54:27.139
Let's hang up. I have a lot to do.

54:30.309 --> 54:31.310
CALL ENDED

54:31.393 --> 54:32.519
That brat.

54:33.687 --> 54:36.190
She's too lazy
to even boil some scorched rice,

54:36.273 --> 54:37.733
and she's cooking up a feast.

54:38.525 --> 54:41.069
Who's coming that she won't tell me?

54:41.612 --> 54:43.280
Is it a guy? [clicks tongue]

54:43.906 --> 54:45.115
I'd be glad if it were.

54:45.199 --> 54:46.658
[seagulls squawking]

54:46.742 --> 54:48.994
Dear seagulls.

54:49.077 --> 54:52.456
If it were someone like that team leader,

54:52.539 --> 54:54.291
wouldn't I be pleased?

54:55.334 --> 54:56.502
Seagulls.

54:59.213 --> 55:00.506
[door closes, beeps]

55:03.550 --> 55:05.052
-[Meri chuckles softly]
-[Kim Wooju gasps]

55:05.135 --> 55:06.553
[♪ enthralling orchestral music laying]

55:14.686 --> 55:15.854
[chuckles nervously]

55:17.439 --> 55:21.443
It's your birthday,
and I wanted to thank you for everything.

55:23.445 --> 55:24.988
-Take a seat.
-Thanks.

55:25.072 --> 55:26.907
Did you prepare all this?

55:27.324 --> 55:29.409
Well, yes, I guess?

55:30.494 --> 55:33.205
This is what I usually eat.

55:36.250 --> 55:38.335
I wanted to empty my fridge,

55:39.253 --> 55:41.880
and I just had to get a few things
and heat them up.

55:41.964 --> 55:44.550
It wasn't that much work.
It was pretty easy. [chuckles softly]

55:44.841 --> 55:46.051
You must be hungry.

55:46.134 --> 55:47.678
-Shall we eat?
-Yes.

55:53.517 --> 55:55.018
-How is it?
-[clears throat]

55:55.352 --> 55:57.896
When we have a guest over,

55:57.980 --> 56:00.023
we serve seaweed soup with octopus.

56:00.107 --> 56:01.275
It's a great energy boost.

56:01.608 --> 56:03.610
[exclaims in realization, chuckles]

56:03.694 --> 56:05.821
That's why it tastes like this.

56:05.904 --> 56:07.114
It's rich, isn't it?

56:07.197 --> 56:08.282
It is.

56:12.661 --> 56:14.246
[♪ whimsical music playing]

56:17.916 --> 56:19.167
[Kim Wooju clears throat]

56:21.211 --> 56:22.212
It's salty.

56:22.879 --> 56:23.880
It's so salty.

56:24.548 --> 56:26.049
[phone vibrating]

56:26.133 --> 56:27.217
[chuckles]

56:27.301 --> 56:28.969
[Youngsook] Just in case you don't know,

56:29.052 --> 56:31.555
don't add extra seasoning to the soup.

56:31.638 --> 56:33.223
The octopus is salty enough.

56:33.557 --> 56:35.392
[Meri] She took her time to tell me that.

56:35.976 --> 56:37.060
[chuckles softly]

56:37.477 --> 56:38.478
The soup is salty.

56:40.022 --> 56:42.983
I should've tasted it
once more at the end.

56:43.066 --> 56:44.526
That's fine. I'll water it down now.

56:47.613 --> 56:48.655
[Kim Wooju chuckles]

56:50.449 --> 56:51.742
[hums in satisfaction, gulps]

56:51.825 --> 56:53.327
-It's perfect.
-[chuckles softly]

56:55.412 --> 56:57.789
I'm sure you had more than enough at home.

56:57.873 --> 57:00.626
Don't eat that. Have something else.

57:00.709 --> 57:01.710
Some japchae.

57:02.252 --> 57:03.962
-[Kim Wooju acknowledges]
-That should be fine.

57:05.631 --> 57:08.550
The braised short ribs are great.
Have some meat, too.

57:10.636 --> 57:12.054
[♪ whimsical sting]

57:16.683 --> 57:18.560
Ms. Yoo, why do you treat me like this?

57:19.561 --> 57:20.562
What?

57:21.104 --> 57:22.939
Why would you cook all this for me?

57:24.066 --> 57:26.109
Even my family
doesn't care about my birthday.

57:28.695 --> 57:29.946
[hesitates]

57:30.030 --> 57:31.990
I didn't know about that.

57:32.741 --> 57:33.867
[exhales]

57:34.576 --> 57:36.495
I haven't had seaweed soup in so long.

57:37.621 --> 57:39.831
[sharp inhale] Was it when I was eight?

57:40.582 --> 57:42.250
I think that was the last time.

57:43.710 --> 57:44.711
I felt like

57:45.462 --> 57:47.005
I shouldn't eat birthday soup.

57:49.883 --> 57:52.678
My parents passed away on my birthday,

57:53.637 --> 57:54.638
and it was my fault.

57:55.138 --> 57:56.640
[♪ ominous sting]

57:56.723 --> 57:59.434
So, instead of having seaweed soup,

57:59.518 --> 58:00.936
I stuffed my face with rice.

58:02.145 --> 58:03.980
Eating lots of rice made me sleepy,

58:04.064 --> 58:05.232
so I could just sleep.

58:05.315 --> 58:06.775
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

58:06.858 --> 58:07.943
When I woke up,

58:08.026 --> 58:09.486
it would be the next day.

58:13.073 --> 58:15.200
That's what I've done to forget that day.

58:18.286 --> 58:19.287
That's why

58:19.913 --> 58:22.916
it feels weird when I see people
who look forward to their birthday.

58:24.626 --> 58:26.878
It feels awkward when someone

58:27.838 --> 58:29.005
wishes me a happy birthday.

58:32.008 --> 58:33.969
Thanks for celebrating with me, though.

58:36.763 --> 58:37.889
[chuckles softly]

58:41.101 --> 58:42.728
[hums in satisfaction, slurps]

58:47.691 --> 58:48.692
Good for you.

58:50.902 --> 58:52.028
For sleeping the whole day.

58:52.654 --> 58:53.655
Good for you.

58:55.282 --> 58:57.701
There are 365 days in a year.

58:57.784 --> 59:00.245
It doesn't matter
if you erase one from your mind.

59:00.787 --> 59:03.915
When things get too tough,
it's best to just run away.

59:04.207 --> 59:05.292
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

59:05.375 --> 59:07.043
Let's eat a lot

59:07.878 --> 59:09.045
and save up our energy.

59:10.297 --> 59:11.298
Okay.

59:18.722 --> 59:19.890
[Kim Wooju hums in satisfaction]

59:19.973 --> 59:20.974
Oh, right.

59:22.142 --> 59:23.727
-[chuckling]
-It's so terribly salty.

59:33.361 --> 59:34.529
-Ms. Yoo.
-Yes?

59:36.072 --> 59:37.073
Right here...

59:37.449 --> 59:38.450
No.

59:38.950 --> 59:40.076
Let me...

59:46.041 --> 59:47.167
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

59:53.632 --> 59:54.758
[clears throat]

59:56.802 --> 59:58.011
When did that happen?

01:00:06.770 --> 01:00:07.771
Hey.

01:00:15.904 --> 01:00:17.489
It's a double rainbow.

01:00:17.572 --> 01:00:18.573
Mr. Kim.

01:00:18.782 --> 01:00:19.908
[♪ enchanting music playing]

01:00:19.991 --> 01:00:21.034
Hurry.

01:00:26.998 --> 01:00:28.083
[exclaims in awe]

01:00:36.967 --> 01:00:37.968
No way.

01:00:42.722 --> 01:00:43.765
[exclaims in awe]

01:00:44.808 --> 01:00:45.851
Quick, make a wish.

01:00:46.476 --> 01:00:47.602
-What?
-What?

01:00:48.061 --> 01:00:50.146
Don't you know
the three best times to make a wish?

01:00:50.230 --> 01:00:52.649
When the first snow falls,
as you hold your breath in a tunnel,

01:00:53.066 --> 01:00:54.067
and to a double rainbow.

01:00:54.150 --> 01:00:55.694
Those wishes come true.

01:00:55.777 --> 01:00:56.987
[scoffing]

01:00:57.070 --> 01:00:58.989
Says who? Who even believes that?

01:01:08.206 --> 01:01:09.541
[♪ enchanting music continues]

01:01:18.091 --> 01:01:19.926
-What did you wish for?
-What about you?

01:01:21.303 --> 01:01:23.346
I wished that everything would work out.

01:01:23.430 --> 01:01:25.181
That I'd make lots of money,

01:01:25.265 --> 01:01:26.725
and that my mom wouldn't get sick.

01:01:26.808 --> 01:01:30.103
I want my career to take off
and no one to find out about the house.

01:01:30.186 --> 01:01:32.480
-Wow, you ask for a lot.
-What did you wish for?

01:01:32.564 --> 01:01:33.899
[hums thoughtfully]

01:01:34.900 --> 01:01:35.901
[clears throat]

01:01:36.318 --> 01:01:37.861
Hey, come on.

01:01:37.944 --> 01:01:38.945
You won't tell?

01:01:39.029 --> 01:01:40.488
[♪ whimsical music playing]

01:01:40.572 --> 01:01:41.615
I don't remember.

01:01:41.698 --> 01:01:42.949
You don't remember?

01:01:43.033 --> 01:01:44.701
Tell me. I want to know.

01:01:44.784 --> 01:01:46.369
Oh, I don't remember.

01:01:46.453 --> 01:01:48.622
You agreed to tell me.

01:01:48.705 --> 01:01:50.707
-When did I say that?
-That didn't work.

01:01:51.833 --> 01:01:53.960
That's not fair. I told you my wishes.

01:01:54.044 --> 01:01:56.546
-Don't ask.
-Then spit out the food you just ate.

01:01:57.547 --> 01:01:58.840
[imitates retching]

01:02:01.009 --> 01:02:03.845
[Kim Wooju] In that short moment,
I made a wish.

01:02:04.721 --> 01:02:06.014
That the wishes of the woman

01:02:06.723 --> 01:02:10.810
who gave me a way out whenever I was
at a dead end would come true.

01:02:29.788 --> 01:02:30.914
Okay, then.

01:02:31.456 --> 01:02:32.791
Tell me if I catch you.

01:02:33.959 --> 01:02:35.335
[♪ dramatic sting]

01:02:37.879 --> 01:02:39.130
[Meri screams, gasps]

01:02:43.593 --> 01:02:45.178
[slow, rhythmic heartbeats]

01:02:48.390 --> 01:02:50.016
[♪ upbeat dreamy music playing]

01:03:58.418 --> 01:04:01.087
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

01:04:01.171 --> 01:04:02.922
[Kim Wooju] Didn't you say
he was in Hong Kong?

01:04:03.006 --> 01:04:04.549
[Meri] Do you think
he came here knowingly?

01:04:04.716 --> 01:04:06.176
[Jingyeong] Thank you for that day.

01:04:06.259 --> 01:04:08.970
[Meri] I want to be with someone
who's there for me when I'm struggling.

01:04:09.054 --> 01:04:10.722
[Sejung] What's this? What do we do?

01:04:10.805 --> 01:04:11.890
[Kim Wooju] We should go.

01:04:11.973 --> 01:04:13.224
[Wooju] ...lives at Beauté Palace.

01:04:13.308 --> 01:04:16.102
I went there for something
and saw someone who looked just like you.

01:04:16.186 --> 01:04:17.645
[Meri] You must've been mistaken.

01:04:17.729 --> 01:04:18.730
Where will you sleep, then?

01:04:18.813 --> 01:04:19.856
That room...

01:04:19.939 --> 01:04:21.649
-[Kim Wooju] I'll sleep here.
-[Meri] What?

01:04:21.733 --> 01:04:23.151
[Jingyeong] Back out of it right now.

01:04:23.234 --> 01:04:25.070
What if your grandmother finds out?

01:04:25.153 --> 01:04:27.155
This makes you an accomplice.

01:04:28.239 --> 01:04:29.365
[Wooju] Did you have fun

01:04:29.449 --> 01:04:31.076
living your fake newlywed life?

01:04:34.454 --> 01:04:36.456
Translated by Jennifer Jean Lim
